# Architecture Rules

## Module structure
New domain → `modules/<name>/{handler,service,repository,routes}` — no other layout.

## Wiring
Wire manually in `cmd/server/main.go`: `repo → service → handler`. Register routes in `internal/server/router.go`.

## Layer responsibilities
- **Handler**: bind request, call service, call `response.*`. No business logic.
- **Service**: all business logic. No GORM, no `c *gin.Context`.
- **Repository**: GORM only. Returns models or errors. No HTTP types.

## Response envelope
Always use `internal/response` — never `c.JSON` directly in handlers.

## Constraints
- No second router framework (only Gin).
- No DI container framework (wire manually).
- No second ORM (only GORM).
- No global state except the logger.
